Make Karto's occupancy grid big enough for its own bounding box.

ComputeDimensions (lib/karto_sdk/include/karto_sdk/Karto.h:6090-6114) sets the
grid to Round(size * scale) cells and the offset to the bounding box MINIMUM,
while WorldToGrid (:4421-4436) indexes with math::Round ABOUT that offset. So for
a point at world x, with u = (x - O)/res, the index is Round(u); u runs over
[0, U] where U = size/res; the largest index produced is Round(U); and the valid
indices are [0, W) with W = Round(U). The last index is therefore one past the
end, and every endpoint in the final half cell of the bounding box is skipped by
TraceLine (:4874-4926, "cells outside the grid are skipped, never clamped") while
the passes along the same ray stop at W-1 and are kept. Passes without hits is
Karto's FREE (UpdateCell, :6244-6256), so the walls that define a map's max-x and
max-y edges can come out free.

+1 is sufficient: it makes the valid range [0, Round(U)], which contains every
index any bounding-box point can produce.
+1 is not more than needed: index Round(U) IS attained, by the extreme point that
set the bounding box, so the added row and column are not dead. +2 would add a
row and column no endpoint and no traced pass could ever reach, and they would
stay Unknown for the life of the grid.

Nothing else needs to change. The offset is untouched, so no existing cell moves:
cell i still has its centre at O + i*res and every index that was valid before is
still the same cell. A map built with this patch therefore differs from one built
without it only by the far row and the far column.

What this does NOT fix, stated so it is not mistaken for a complete claim: a
reading at or above rangeThreshold is rescaled to exactly rangeThreshold along its
own beam (AddScan, :6173-6179) and that synthesised endpoint is NOT a bounding-box
point -- the box is built from the sensor pose and the FILTERED readings only
(:5696-5700 over m_PointReadings, filtered at :5662 by
InRange(r, minRange, rangeThreshold)), while AddScan traces
GetPointReadings(false) = the unfiltered ones (:5613-5623). No change to
ComputeDimensions can bound those. They carry isEndPointValid = false (:6167) and
so can only ever mark free space, never a hit, which is why losing their tails
costs free-space marking and never a wall.

Against: ros-jazzy-slam-toolbox 2.8.5, orig tarball SHA256
80af3955a610a81c320b4a75bff6b5e5ca99a6118455b7ca5ee1530e25608583.
Apply with -p1 from the package root (the directory holding package.xml).

NOT APPLIED to ~/src/slam_toolbox_2.8.5, which stays pristine so that every line
number cited in docs/specs/ keeps resolving. See the Option A plan in
SPEC_b2_wall_predicate §12.7: the overlay patches a COPY.

--- a/lib/karto_sdk/include/karto_sdk/Karto.h
+++ b/lib/karto_sdk/include/karto_sdk/Karto.h
@@ -6108,8 +6108,11 @@
     kt_double scale = 1.0 / resolution;
     Size2<kt_double> size = boundingBox.GetSize();
 
-    rWidth = static_cast<kt_int32s>(math::Round(size.GetWidth() * scale));
-    rHeight = static_cast<kt_int32s>(math::Round(size.GetHeight() * scale));
+    // +1: WorldToGrid rounds about rOffset, so a point at the far end of the
+    // bounding box indexes to Round(size*scale), which is one past the end of a
+    // Round(size*scale)-cell grid. See docs/patches/karto_extent.patch.
+    rWidth = static_cast<kt_int32s>(math::Round(size.GetWidth() * scale)) + 1;
+    rHeight = static_cast<kt_int32s>(math::Round(size.GetHeight() * scale)) + 1;
     rOffset = boundingBox.GetMinimum();
   }
 
